          alt: "Nasogastric tube — measuring and confirming. Measuring the length — NEX: nose, ear lobe, xiphisternum; mark the tube, then insert to that mark. Confirming position: 1 aspirate and test on pH paper — pH 5.5 or below is safe to use; 2 if in doubt, X-ray — the definitive check; never feed until position is confirmed. The discarded test — why 'push air and listen' is unsafe: a tube in the lung, the oesophagus or curled in the mouth can all produce a convincing bubbling sound over the stomach; the test cannot tell them apart; feed delivered into a lung is frequently fatal, so the whoosh test has been abandoned in favour of pH testing and X-ray. During insertion: sit upright, head slightly flexed forward — flexion closes the airway and opens the oesophagus; ask the patient to swallow sips of water as you advance; coughing, choking or colour change means withdraw at once; head back and extended points the tube towards the trachea — the commonest positioning error.",
