        "Tracheostomy care is a bedhead sign with tube details and the algorithm, inner cannula care every 4–8 hours, a keyhole dressing and ties changed daily by two people with one finger's slack, continuous humidification, measured shallow suction under 15 seconds, cuff pressure 20–30 cmH₂O with full deflation before any speaking valve, the first change not before day 4 (surgical) or 7–10 (percutaneous), communication aids and family teaching; the emergency algorithm is call for help, oxygen to face and stoma, remove the valve and inner cannula, pass a suction catheter, deflate the cuff, remove the tube, oxygenate by face or stoma, and reintubate orally or through the stoma — with the laryngectomy patient oxygenated only through the stoma.",
        "Nasogastric tubes are measured nose–ear–xiphisternum, inserted with the head flexed, confirmed by fresh aspirate pH 5.5 or below and by X-ray before the first feed and after any doubt — never by the whoosh test — with the external length recorded each shift; drugs by tube are given separately with 30 mL flushes, liquid where possible, never crushed modified-release or enteric-coated tablets, and separated from feed for phenytoin, ciprofloxacin and levothyroxine.",
