            "<strong>Infection</strong>: the ICU nurse's own TB exposure from the ventilated patient with undiagnosed disease, the viral haemorrhagic fever that arrives as 'malaria not responding', the COVID-19 of 2020–21 that killed health workers in every country — the N95 fitted and worn for aerosol-generating procedures, the index of suspicion, the occupational health screening, and the right to refuse to work without PPE.",
